From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: vvc1: remove() stops the recycle timer before it cancels the error
 work

Found in review, traced in the code. amvdec_vc1_remove() cancelled
error_wd_work first and deleted the recycle timer only after amvdec_stop()
and the IRQ free. The timer is what queues that work (VC1_SOS_COUNT > 10,
the decoder's error state), so it could queue it again in between, and
error_do_work then ran after remove: amvdec_stop, vf_light_unreg_provider,
vvc1_local_init (canvases on the buffers decoder_bmmu_box_free has freed),
vf_reg_provider, amvdec_start - firmware DMA into freed CMA, a reset of the
next decoder on VDEC_1, and a stale provider registered. Closing a VC-1
title while it was in that error state was enough.

The timer is now deleted first, then the work cancelled: nothing can queue
it again.
---
 drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c
index cf1a0d8..e66bfde 100644
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c
@@ -1896,6 +1896,15 @@ static int amvdec_vc1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static int amvdec_vc1_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	/* The recycle timer is what queues error_wd_work (VC1_SOS_COUNT > 10),
+	 * so it goes first: cancelled before it, the work could be queued again
+	 * and run after this - restarting the firmware on freed buffers, with
+	 * the provider registered again.
+	 */
+	if (stat & STAT_TIMER_ARM) {
+		del_timer_sync(&recycle_timer);
+		stat &= ~STAT_TIMER_ARM;
+	}
 	cancel_work_sync(&error_wd_work);
 	vc1_print(0, VC1_DEBUG_DETAIL,"%s \n", __func__);
 	if (stat & STAT_VDEC_RUN) {
@@ -1909,11 +1918,6 @@ static int amvdec_vc1_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		stat &= ~STAT_ISR_REG;
 	}
 
-	if (stat & STAT_TIMER_ARM) {
-		del_timer_sync(&recycle_timer);
-		stat &= ~STAT_TIMER_ARM;
-	}
-
 	cancel_work_sync(&set_clk_work);
 	if (stat & STAT_VF_HOOK) {
 		if (!is_reset)
